# New Feature: Age_Group
# Feature description: Categorizes individuals into age groups such as young adult (18-25), adult (26-40), middle-aged (41-60), senior (60+).
# Usefulness: Age often impacts creditworthiness and credit card application approval; younger individuals may be less likely to qualify due to lower employment history or income stability, while middle-aged individuals typically have greater earning potential. Categorization can help a model better capture age-related trends.
df['Age_Group'] = pd.cut(
    df['Age'], 
    bins=[15.75, 25, 40, 60, 76.75], 
    labels=['Young Adult', 'Adult', 'Middle Aged', 'Senior'], 
    include_lowest=True
)
df = pd.get_dummies(df, columns=['Age_Group'], drop_first=True)
end

python
# New Feature: Debt-to-Income Ratio (DTI)
# Feature description: Calculates the ratio of debt to income as a new feature: Debt / (Income + 1). A small offset (+1) is added to avoid division errors when income is zero.
# Usefulness: This ratio is a major determinant in credit card approvals. High debt combined with low income would indicate an individual may be a risky borrower, whereas low DTI is often associated with better creditworthiness.
df['Debt_Income_Ratio'] = df['Debt'] / (df['Income'] + 1)
end

python
# New Feature: Employment Stability Index
# Feature description: Combines YearsEmployed and Employed status into a single feature using the formula: Index = YearsEmployed * Employed. For individuals employed (Employed=1), this feature reflects tenure; for those unemployed (Employed=0), it’s simply zero.
# Usefulness: This feature captures the combined impact of job stability and employment status. Long tenures are positively correlated with financial stability and increase the likelihood of credit card approval.
df['Employment_Stability_Index'] = df['YearsEmployed'] * df['Employed']
end

